RFC 7208 sets no length limit on a single literal, mechanism, modifier
or explanation, but a literal past 255 chars or a value compiling past
511 bytes made the record a permerror (an explanation: the default
text). A long literal now continues in further string blocks and the
compile buffers are sized from the value; only the whole-record limits
remain. The record printer read two chars past a literal ending in %
(or %2), which in a heap buffer is uninitialised padding.

